# Copy to .env.local, fill in real tokens, then:
#   bash:       set -a; source .env.local; set +a; bash scripts/setup-mcp-servers.sh
#   cmd/batch:  scripts\setup-mcp-servers.bat .env.local
# Do NOT commit .env.local — add it to .gitignore.

# --- GitHub bot PATs (all required) ---
ORCHESTRATOR_BOT_GITHUB_PAT=
BACKEND_BOT_GITHUB_PAT=
FRONTEND_BOT_GITHUB_PAT=
REVIEWER_BOT_GITHUB_PAT=
QA_BOT_GITHUB_PAT=

# --- Jira / Atlassian ---
# Nothing to put here. The Jira servers use OAuth, so the setup script
# registers them without credentials and you authenticate interactively:
#
#   claude  ->  /mcp  ->  pick the alias  ->  Authenticate
#
# Do the four aliases one at a time, each browser consent completed while
# logged into that bot's Atlassian account (use a private window between
# them — one Atlassian session per browser at a time):
#
#   jira-orchestrator -> pipeline-orchestrator-bot  (transitions, comments)
#   jira-ba           -> pipeline-ba-bot            (creates stories)
#   jira-research     -> pipeline-research-bot      (read-only)
#   jira-qa           -> pipeline-qa-bot            (read-only)
#
# jira-ba is only used in requirements mode (REQUIREMENTS_MODE in CLAUDE.md).
# If you always start runs from an existing ticket, you can leave it
# unauthenticated.
#
# Each bot's Jira permissions are granted in Jira itself, not here.
